                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Played On: [b]HTC Vive[/b][/h1]\n\nRoadRunner VR is just what its name suggests; you run down a never-ending road in VR. You do this automatically, while using the left and right buttons on the trackpad to move back and forth to collect gems, rockets, hearts, and jetpacks. The gems only add to your total score, the hearts restore your health if you've hit an object, and the rockets can blast obstacles out of your way or be used to shoot down the occasional UFO that comes by to scoop up the gems. I never found a use for the jetpacks, if there is one then the game doesn't tell you how to use it and none of the buttons I pressed activated it. Even though it says that you can physically move to change lanes, I didn't find that any amount of movement changed my position on the screen; I was still able to get hit by things and pick up items by leaning left and right, though. It's a broken release, and it has very little content. It might be good for a kid, but there's still better out there.\n\n[h1]Rating: [b]0.5/5.0[/b] - Abysmal, avoid it like the plague.[/h1]\nThe VR Network [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33182845-The-VR-Network/]Curator[/url] | [url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/thevrnetwork]Group[/url] Click for More\n\n[b]The developer provided a free copy of this game for review, through The VR Network's Curation page.[/b]",
